.Dd March 18, 2026
.Dt VIRTIO_GPU 4
.Os Substrate
.Sh NAME
.Nm virtio_gpu
.Nd VirtIO GPU legacy PCI transport driver
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Cd "device virtio_gpu"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
driver attaches to transitional VirtIO GPU PCI devices and performs the
transport-level initialization required for later display use.
.Pp
At this stage, the driver:
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
matches the VirtIO GPU PCI device
.It
obtains the legacy I/O BAR
.It
resets and acknowledges the device
.It
allocates the control and cursor virtqueues
.It
transitions the device to
.Dv DRIVER_OK
.El
.Pp
The driver can create a basic 2D resource, attach a single backing entry, and
bind that resource to scanout 0.
It does not yet query display modes, transfer dirty rectangles to the host, or
upload cursor images.
.Sh HARDWARE
The
.Nm
driver supports transitional VirtIO GPU devices with vendor ID
.Li 0x1af4
and PCI device ID
.Li 0x1010 .
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Pa
.It Pa sys/drivers/virtio/virtio.c
PCI driver-model registration.
.It Pa sys/drivers/virtio/virtio_gpu.c
VirtIO GPU transport setup.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr fb 4 ,
.Xr vga 4
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
driver first appeared in Substrate.
